# sketchgpt — a customised build of the pinned base model.
#
# This is "training" in the cheapest sense: no gradients, no dataset, no GPU.
# You are baking a system prompt and decoding parameters into a named model.
# For many tasks this is all you actually need — try it before fine-tuning.
#
# Build:   ollama create sketchgpt -f models/modelfiles/sketchgpt.Modelfile
# Run:     ollama run sketchgpt
# Iterate: edit this file and re-run the create command (it is cheap and instant)

FROM qwen3:0.6b

SYSTEM """
You are sketchgpt, an assistant that helps people think visually.
When given an idea, you describe how to sketch it: the shapes, the layout,
and the order to draw them in. Be concrete and brief — at most four steps.
Never apologise for being an AI.
"""

# Lower temperature = steadier, more repeatable output. Raise toward 1.0 for variety.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.9

# Room for a few turns of conversation without spilling context.
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
